    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Description\n\nWhen calling `goto_hunk`, if wrapping is not enabled and there are [no further hunks](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/diff.lua#L778) then the value of `H.notify` is returned but the wrapper does not [return anything](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/diff.lua#L1784). Would you be in favour of returning the the output of `vim.notify` here?\n\nMy use case:\nSometimes I like to cycle through all changes I have made, without using something like diffview.nvim. What I would like to do in this case is grab all files with changes and then traverse through all hunks. This requires knowing when the last hunk in a file has been reached, though I realise my proposal is effectively a presence check, and is subject to much brittleness. If there is any other way to get this information please let me know!",
